    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Chloride-responsive: 0.9% saline IV, typically 50 to 100 mL/hour above urinary and other losses, until urinary Cl > 25 mEq/L and urinary pH normalizes."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Chloride-unresponsive: rarely benefits from rehydration alone; tx the specific cause; K and Mg supplementation and/or K-sparing diuretics are usually needed."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Acetazolamide 250 to 375 mg PO or IV once or twice a day increases HCO3 excretion but may accelerate urinary K and phosphate losses."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Acetazolamide may especially benefit volume-overloaded pts w diuretic-induced or posthypercapnic metabolic alkalosis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Severe (pH > 7.6) w kidney failure when dialysis can't or shouldn't be done: HCl 0.1 to 0.2 normal solution IV, only through a central catheter (hyperosmotic; scleroses peripheral veins)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
